Given,
$\begin{aligned}
& i=10 \mathrm{ A}, B=0.15 \mathrm{ T}, \\
& \theta=45^{{}^{\circ}} \text{$ and $} l=2 \mathrm{ m}
\end{aligned}$
Here, $F=i l B \sin \theta=10 \times 2 \times 0.15 \sin 45^{{}^{\circ}}=\frac{3}{\sqrt{2}} \mathrm{ N}$

Force on $25 \mathrm{ cm}$ length of wire $C$ due to wire $D$ is
$\begin{aligned}
F_{D} &=\frac{\mu_{0}}{4 \pi} \frac{2 \bar{I}_{1} I_{2}}{r} \times l \\
&=10^{-7} \times \frac{30 \times 10 \times 2}{3 \times 10^{-2}} \times 25 \times 10^{-2} \\
&=5 \times 10^{-4} \mathrm{ N}, \text{ towards \right}
\end{aligned}$
Force of $25 \mathrm{ cm}$ length of wire $C$ due to wire $G$ is
$\begin{aligned}
F_{G} &=10^{-7} \times \frac{2 \times 20 \times 10}{2 \times 10^{-2}} \times 25 \times 10^{-2} \\
&=5 \times 10^{-4} \mathrm{ N}, \text{ towards left }
\end{aligned}\therefore$ Net force on wire $C=F_{D}-F_{G}=0$

Magnetic moment of a coil of area A carrying current $I$ is given by
$\begin{aligned}
M &=I A \\
\Rightarrow \text{ Current, } I &=\frac{M}{A}
\end{aligned}$

Magnetic field strength $B$ due to long straight current carrying conductor at a distance $r$ is given as $\begin{aligned} B \text{$ and $} =\frac{\mu_{0}}{2 \pi} \cdot \frac{I}{r}\\
\Rightarrow \quad \text{ and } B \propto \frac{1}{r}
\end{aligned}$ Hence, correct variation of $B$ with $r$ is shown in the graph given in option (c).
